    "updated_at": "2017-08-17T19:53:11Z",
    "body": "My newly-updated tests indicate that Edge seems to expose frameset normally but not inside an iframe, but other browsers expose in both cases.  Yet somehow all browsers do pass the relevant test at <http://w3c-test.org/html/browsers/the-window-object/named-access-on-the-window-object/named-objects.html>?  I don't get it, what's happening here?\r\n\r\nPing @cdumez because he made the relevant test change.",
