    "updated_at": "2017-08-18T07:59:29Z",
    "body": "I think I found the source of the confusion. The definition of Window's named properties and named objects got out of sync when @domenic made that change and nobody noticed thus far. The \"Named objects\" definition hasn't changed since Ian was doing all the writing and is the one that still contains `a` and `area`. A bit above it is the named properties definition which doesn't have them.\r\n\r\nI don't immediately see a good way to deduplicate those two structures though.",
